The three scripts commit 23 ran, with what each found, for the review (Phase 5): at-imports.mjs,
amendment 4 (c)'s codemod (a relative import or re-export that leaves its feature or its top
folder of src becomes an @/ path; import lines only; 77 specifiers in 48 files, at-imports.tsv);
unused-exports.mjs, R1.9.27's sweep (exports with no importer outside their module, mock factory
keys and requireActual reads counted, Next.js special files, 'use server' modules and the frozen
files skipped; 47 rows, unused-exports.tsv: 44 lost `export`, 3 used nowhere were deleted); and
zone-probes.mjs, §1.7.4's proof that each layered zone fires (eslint's lintText on 35 probe
paths, nothing written; zone-probes.txt, 0 wrong).

